{% doc %}
  The address of an event's own page, when it has one to show (DS-176). Prints nothing when it
  hasn't, so a caller links the event as it did before.

  An event has a page of its own once the store shows the event entry type as web pages, which
  waits for release. Until then every event's address is blank and this prints nothing. After
  that, an event with a summary has a page worth opening. One without a summary has a page that
  would hold a title, a date and a room, so its rows keep linking to its programme.

  Capture the output and strip it.

  @param {object} event - An event entry

  @example
  {%- capture own_page -%}{% render 'gs-event-page-link', event: event %}{%- endcapture -%}
  {%- assign own_page = own_page | strip -%}
{% enddoc %}
{%- if event.system.url != blank and event.summary.value != blank -%}
  {{- event.system.url -}}
{%- endif -%}
